# AgentSlice Rules

Follow `AGENT_RULES.md`. Before editing, read `agentslice.policy.json`, confirm its canonical workspace matches the Git root, then read only `AGENT_RULES.md`, active context, workflow state, and current slice. Use the archive index only for a concrete historical need.

Ask for the concrete current user problem. A local `explore/<idea>` branch is short, reversible, and never gets a PR, Vercel preview, spec, QA record, checkpoint, merge, or deployment. Promote sensitive policy areas—auth/ownership, database/RLS, public contracts/pages, integrations, commerce, hosting, CI, or production data—promptly to `controlled-change`.

Every formal PR has exactly one lane: `docs`, `fast-bug`, `standard-feature`, or `controlled-change`. The PR is the live source for status, QA, decision, and rollback. CI validates the lane marker, sensitive paths, and fast-bug's application-file limit when the PR or its body changes. Read only task-specific inputs; never bulk-read history.

Keep the formal gates: human scope approval; human controlled plan/spec approval; independent QA `PASS`/`PASS WITH NOTES`; human release approval. Default QA to focused acceptance/domain regression plus lint/typecheck for code. Broaden checks only for the stated risk trigger. Keep docs short, archive closed document-led history with redirects, and do not parallelize by default.
